## Steps for .data file
#### 1. Create `(.pdb)` file for a single molecule  --> `h2o.pdb`, `K.pdb`, `Cl.pdb`

```
HEADER    water
COMPND
SOURCE
HETATM    1  H   HOH     1       4.225   5.600  5.000
HETATM    2  H   HOH     1       5.775   5.600  5.000
HETATM    3  O   HOH     1       5.000   5.000  5.000
CONECT    1    3
CONECT    2    3
CONECT    3    1    2
END
```

```
HETATM    1  K   POT     1       0.000   0.000   0.000
END
```

```
HETATM    1  CL  CLA     1       0.000   0.000   0.000
END
```

#### 2. Write a `fill.inp` file and use in UBUNTU ```packmol < fill.inp```. This will give a (.pdb) file containing bunch of molecules.

```
tolerance 2.0
filetype pdb
output water_kcl.pdb
add_box_sides 1.0 

structure h2o.pdb
  number 33000
  inside box 0. 0. 0. 100. 100. 100.
end structure

structure K.pdb
  number 60
  inside box 0. 0. 0. 100. 100. 100.
end structure

structure Cl.pdb
  number 60
  inside box 0. 0. 0. 100. 100. 100.
end structure
```


#### 3. Using `VMD`, open TK console and input these commands

```
package require topotools
topo guessatom element mass
topo guessbonds
topo guessangles
topo writelammpsdata F:\\sla_hiwi\\lammps_testRuns\\h2o_KCl\\packmol_files\\water_kcl.data full

```
